  "CHEESEY TRIPPY - Hybrid Retail Programme/2. Site Analysis": {
    "images": [
      {
        "file": "Watercolor Urban Site Analysis Map.png",
        "title": "Site Analysis",
        "description": "Nashik is the \"Wine Capital of India\" and the consumption of wine is also the most in Nashik. The wines have high acidity and a good acid-sugar balance. Nashik has an ideal temperature variation, particularly in winters, that helps grapes retain acidity and optimal sugar levels. The maximum age group of people living in college road area is between 20 to 24 years. According to youth wine can easily bring some kind of pleasure not only to your taste buds but also to your sense of sight, as well as your sense of smell. This is the main reason to open store near this area. As Nashik is the main hub for manufacturing of wine we can easily deliver online orders of customers and the selling of wine and cheese will increase.\n\nJUSTIFICATION\nNashik is the fourth largest city in Maharashtra. Length=1.52kms.\nNearest Airport: Shirdhi Airport, 57.69kms\nNearest Railway Station: Nashik Road, 8.19k.\nConnected Major Roads: Gajanan Janardhan, Mhatre Road, Canada Corner Link Road, Canal Link Road, BYK Playground Ring Road, Thatte Nagar Road.\nThere were 22 wineries in Nashik, out of 46 wineries throughout India. The largest vineyard in Nashik is the Sula Vineyards.\nCommercial Stores: Apparel, Offices & Industries, University, Restaurant, Electronics store, Pharmacy, Café, Hospital, Mise, Education, Coaching."
      }
